# Write clear titles

<h2 id="wg-030">Name the action and its object</h2>

Start a control label with a verb and say what it affects. Make repeated labels different from each other.

Titles must also be unique and make sense on their own, so keep them short. Aim for 65 characters or fewer for a page title. Do not shorten a room name or drop a condition to fit.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Submit | Save schedule |
| On | Turn on reading lamp |
| Settings (on five cards) | Lounge lamp settings |
| Entity management and configuration options | Change a device name |

Use “Continue” only for a real next step. Use sentence case: “Save schedule”, not “Save Schedule”. Use words the household uses, not the integration’s internal name. Do not make the label longer just to rename a native control.
